 ## Overview
-Slice Parallelisation is a parallelisation scheme for Coherent Grid Traversal (CGT) where processing elements are assigned to slices of the volume rather than individual rays or bundles [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of determining which ray bundles intersect a given slice when traversal is not incremental, requiring explicit data structures to map bundles to slices [S1, S2, unofficial]. Unlike Bundle Parallelisation, it reduces redundant block fetches from neighbouring bundles by organizing work per slice [S1, S2, unofficial].
