 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Cache Locality:** If vectors $A$ and $D$ fit in cache/local store, identifying bundles for a slice requires 0 memory reads beyond the cache. If they do not fit, exactly 2 memory reads are required to fetch the relevant index tables [S1, S2, unofficial].
-*   **Redundant Fetches:** While Slice Parallelisation is less likely to exhibit redundant block fetches from neighbouring bundles compared to other methods, it is still possible [S1, S2, unofficial].
-*   **Roll Angle:** When the "roll" angle of the bundles relative to the volume angle is close to $\pi/4$, the number of block fetches can double [S1, S2, unofficial]. A solution is noted as "not yet published" in the source [S1, S2, unofficial].
